  "summary": "Eight preprints show protein and genomic language models being adapted with dynamics, structure and reference-based inputs for variant, enzyme and homology tasks.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is adapting pretrained sequence models to specific prediction tasks by adding auxiliary information rather than scaling alone. DynamicsPLM adds molecular dynamics heads to a 35M-parameter model for zero-shot variant effects, and MicroDUET attaches phylogeny and function adapter heads to a compact genomic model. HieraPTM combines sequence, language model and 3D structure features for functional phosphosite prediction. EnzRef models reactants and products against a frozen model for kcat, while SMSTPred uses embeddings for methyltransferase substrate specificity. FoldMapper uses structure-derived evolutionary profiles for inverse folding, and S-PLM-TM targets remote homology search. The benchmarking study finds anisotropy impairs embedding retrieval against MMseqs2 and Foldseek, with ZCA whitening as a remedy.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
